<title>CANADA: CWB details railcar unloads at export position.</title>
<headline>CWB details railcar unloads at export position.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board on Monday detailed the number of railcar unloads at export position for the week ended Nov 3.</p>
<p>As many as 3,549 hopper cars were unloaded at Vancouver, exceeding the weekly target of 3,400, the CWB statement said.</p>
<p>There were 1,186 hopper cars unloaded in Prince Rupert, below the weekly target of 1,500. Thunder Bay saw 2,695 hopper cars, beneath the weekly 3,000 target, and Churchill saw 237 grain cars, beneath the weekly 300 hopper car target.</p>
<p>Primary elevator space across the Prairies were not yet available.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
